 "notes": "Fig.6 top panel, linear photon coupling d_gamma^(1). Paper Eq.(6) defines L=(kappa phi)^n(d_gamma^(n)(1/4)F F - d_me^(n) m_e ebar e) with kappa=1/(sqrt(2)M_P)=sqrt(4pi)/M_Pl, so d_gamma^(1) equals the Damour-Donoghue d_e (Delta alpha/alpha = d_e kappa phi). Curve traced from the light-red Yb+/Sr 95% C.L. spectrum (upper envelope per mass bin); dark-red is the best-fit spectrum, black-dashed is expected-noise (excluded as sensitivity). Excluded region is above the curve. ULDM assumes scalar saturates local density rho_DM=0.3 GeV/cm^3 (Sec 5; paper notes 0.4 gives negligible difference). Mass range ~1e-20 to 8e-17 eV (freq 1e-6-2e-2 Hz). Linear-coupling stochastic degradation factor ~3 already applied by paper. Paper notes Ref.[25] Yb+/Sr clocks claim slightly tighter limits, but this is the paper own measured bound.",
